      "criterion": "Explicit Quality/Governance/source authority, independent actual execution identity and single use",
      "decision": "accepted",
      "assessment": "Quality intersects explicit Governance and inherited InputAuthority source; candidate/manual/marked/unknown paths do not gain auto authority. Execution requires the actual registered Session on an independent QA Task. New capture_origin, reserved report IDs and a nonempty exact digest close the earlier bypasses. Independent probes cover foreign Runtime sessions, actor mismatch, after-commit expiry and after-run Task revision change.",
      "suite_run": "m3_suite",
      "additional_runs": [
        "independent_boundaries",
        "fresh_demo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Crash, result rollback and global recovery without rerun",
      "decision": "accepted",
      "assessment": "Durable dispatch and ResourceGate serialize actual execution. SQLite failure at report insertion rolls back the entire result batch, leaving in_flight for bounded no-rerun recovery. The full M3 suite includes real process crash (exit 73), process contention and one-use concurrency; embedded Verification actions participate in global recovery.",
      "suite_run": "m3_suite",
      "additional_runs": [
        "independent_boundaries",
        "fresh_demo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Receipt/report/terminal integrity, atomic cursor and pure old/new Replay",
      "decision": "accepted",
      "assessment": "Reducers bind receipt, Command, capture origin, report and terminal facts; bad events preserve State and cursor. Independent probes reseal origin and change the embedded report Command. All 8 frozen full/facts stores replayed across 530 prefixes with 26 zero-call guards and unchanged bytes; 6 legacy states match their original complete-state digests. The fresh independent demo adds 2 new stores and 170 prefixes with 24 zero-call guards.",
      "suite_run": "m3_suite",
      "additional_runs": [
        "independent_boundaries",
